@startuml

title A derived market object: the states of a set

[*] --> Candidate : compute
Candidate --> Candidate : compute again\n(a new version)
Candidate --> Raised : raise a publish\n(names the version)
Raised --> Approved : decided yes,\nor closed by a stated rule
Raised --> Closed : refused, withdrawn\nor expired
Approved --> Published : the trader applies\n(the version is the one approved)
Approved --> Closed : the candidate changed,\nso the apply is refused
Published --> Superseded : a newer set of the\nseries is applied
Published --> Withdrawn : a withdrawal is\napproved and applied
Superseded --> [*]
Withdrawn --> [*]
Closed --> [*]

Candidate : stored, versioned, traceable
Candidate : not consumable
Raised : one open request\nper subject and as-of
Published : the live set of its series
Superseded : still the set for\nan as-of before its successor
Withdrawn : no reader takes it
Closed : nothing was published

@enduml
